videos.script:
A friend sends you a link to a course in the planner. You tap it in a chat. {{tap}} Does the planner open, on that course? Or does a browser open a web page?

That decision is not the app's. The system makes it, before your code runs at all. {{system}} A link with the app's own scheme opens any app that claims that scheme, and anyone can claim it. {{scheme}} An ordinary web address opens the app only when the website says, in a file of its own, that this app may. {{verified}}

Today you write the planner's side of both. A parser that turns a link into a screen and refuses everything else. {{parser}} And a tiny web server that serves the two files Android and iOS fetch, with the headers they check. {{server}} Then the case nobody tests: the app is not installed, and the link has to work anyway.
